  "id": "812ca358-35c9-51b0-bd97-64af5650cfb4",
  "slug": "squash-relish",
  "name": "Squash Relish",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This squash relish recipe is made with yellow summer squash and bell peppers in a sweet-tangy pickling liquid for a colorful, refreshing condiment.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place squash, onion, and bell peppers in a large bowl; sprinkle with salt and toss to coat. Set aside to drain for 1 hour. Discard liquid."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Place sugar, vinegar, celery seeds, and mustard seeds in a large pot; bring to a boil over medium heat, stirring to dissolve sugar. Stir in squash mixture and return to a boil; cook until vegetables are tender, about 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Inspect 6 pint-sized jars for cracks and rings for rust, discarding any defective ones. Immerse in simmering water until relish is ready. Wash new, unused lids and rings in warm soapy water."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Pack relish into hot, sterilized jars, filling to within \u00bc-inch of tops. Run a clean knife or thin spatula around insides of jars to remove any air bubbles. Wipe rims with a moist paper towel to remove any residue. Top with lids and screw rings on tightly."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Place a rack in the bottom of a large stockpot and fill halfway with water. Bring to a boil and lower jars 2 inches apart into the boiling water using a holder. Pour in more boiling water to cover jars by at least 1 inch. Bring to a rolling boil, cover, and process for 10 minutes, or the time recommended for your location."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Remove the jars from the stockpot; place onto a cloth-covered or wood surface, several inches apart, until cool. Press centers of lids with a finger to ensure lids do not move up or down. Store in a cool, dark area."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 192,
